# Predicting Vehicle Fuel Efficiency and CO2 Emission Using Regression Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview

This project uses machine learning regression techniques to predict vehicle fuel efficiency and CO2 emissions based on historical vehicle data. The project focuses on data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis, feature engineering, model training, and performance evaluation.

## 🎯 Objectives

* Predict vehicle fuel efficiency using regression analysis.
* Analyze factors that influence CO2 emissions.
* Apply data preprocessing and feature engineering techniques.
* Train and compare machine learning regression models.
* Evaluate model performance using appropriate regression metrics.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Seaborn
* Scikit-learn
* Jupyter Notebook

## 📊 Machine Learning Workflow

1. Data Collection
2. Data Cleaning
3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
4. Feature Engineering
5. Train-Test Split
6. Model Training
7. Model Evaluation
8. Model Comparison
9. Prediction

## 🤖 Models Used

* Linear Regression
* Decision Tree Regression
* Random Forest Regression
* Other regression algorithms as applicable

## 📈 Model Evaluation

The models are evaluated using regression metrics such as:

* R² Score
* Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
* Mean Squared Error (MSE)
* Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)

